  "final_message": "Declined payments are now retried on schedule, and a card that keeps declining ends the subscription `unpaid`.\n\n**Root cause:** `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py` filtered invoices on `invoice[\"status\"] == \"opened\"`. Invoice status is never `\"opened\"`; the valid literal is `\"open\"` (see `InvoiceStatus` in `billing/models.py`, and every other status check in the codebase). So the filter matched nothing, `run_cycle` never called `payments.collect` on a due invoice, and `attempt_count` stayed at 1. The subscription remained `past_due` with a stale `next_attempt_at`.\n\n**Fix:** changed the literal to `\"open\"` in `due_for_retry`, one line.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Added `tests/test_dunning.py` with two tests:\n  - A declined first charge is retried at day 1, and the subscription returns to `active`.\n  - A card that keeps declining makes four attempts (initial plus retries at days 1, 3 and 7), then the subscription goes `unpaid` with `next_attempt_at` cleared.\n- Both new tests failed before the fix, with `attempt_count == 1`.\n- Full suite: 26 passed (`.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q`).\n\n**Answer file:** `answer.json` at the repo root contains `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.\n\nNothing is committed. The changes are in `billing/dunning.py`, the new `tests/test_dunning.py`, and `answer.json`.",
